 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeaRtl0Gfls/",
 "title": "Execution Beats Perfection",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "Chris Lavin demonstrates the importance of taking action quickly rather than waiting for certainty. He explains that executing on many things with 90% accuracy yields far better results than executing on only one thing with 100% accuracy.",
 "key_points": [
  "The creator demonstrates this with an example where he offers to sell a $5 bill for $1 with a 10-second deadline.",
  "Only two people in the audience took action and claimed the $5 bill.",
  "There are three kinds of people: those who make things happen, those who watch things happen, and those who wonder what happened.",
  "The creator attributes his success to execution and executing quickly.",
  "The creator claims he may be right 90% of the time and wrong 10% of the time.",
  "Executing on 100 things and being right 90% of the time gives you 90 accomplishments.",
  "Being right 100% of the time but only executing on one thing gives you only one accomplishment."
 ],
 "content": "Most people watched a $5 bill sell for $1 and did nothing. Speed beats perfect. Chris executes on 100 things at 90% and wins 90. Waiting for certainty gets you one. Follow @thechrislavin to learn more. I have a $5 bill I'm going to sell for a dollar. Does that interest anyone? Good for 10 seconds then the deal expires. 10, 9, 8, 7, be careful, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, there you go. Give her a round of applause. I hope you are learning from this. I hope you're a student ready to to see what happened here. Two people did something that most of you didn't even try to do. What did they do? They took action. Thinkers, three kinds of people, those who make things happen, those who watch things happen, and those who are still going what happened. No, but it's action that makes all the difference in the world. This is near and dear to me because the reason that I am where I am is because I actually execute. I execute, I execute quickly. I was just on a call with my sales team for another business and I was like execute, execute, execute. That's the reality. I maybe right 90% of the time, I may be wrong 10% of the time. But I'll tell you what, if you execute on 100 things and you're right 90% of the time, you got 90. If you're right 100% of the of the time and only execute on one, you've only accomplished one thing. I'm here to tell you execute, execute, execute. My partner constantly comments on how fast I make things happen. That's the way to live life.",
 "status": "done",
